@using Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection
@using Microsoft.JSInterop
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Metrics
@implements IDisposable
@inject IAgentSessionSource Sessions
@inject IDeliveryRunSource Runs
@inject IServiceProvider Services
@inject IJSRuntime JS

@*
    The sessions pane: the Claude and Copilot sessions this environment has a record
    of. The Sessions context's only list of them (see .devbook/domain/sessions/,
    "The session list and its detail").

    A filter bar, a list, and a detail panel beside it. The list answers "what have
    my agents been doing here" at a glance — one row per session, saying who ran it,
    where, on which model at which effort, how far its run got — and the panel
    answers "what exactly happened in this one" without the row growing into a
    report. A panel beside the list rather than a page of its own, because a reader
    is usually moving down the rows, and a panel keeps their place. At a narrow width
    the panel drops under the list.

    It was first built as a second pane on Dev PC Management, which read plausibly
    and was wrong about the boundary: one is how a PC is configured, the other is what
    has been running on it, for how long and in which repository. Like the tools pane
    it owns its own loading; the shell decides whether there is a sessions pane, and
    this decides what is in one.

    Two things this pane deliberately is not.

    It is not a monitor. It reads the folders once when it opens and again when
    somebody asks, and there is no timer. A Copilot session leaves no liveness marker
    at all, so a list that moved by itself would move without meaning.

    It is not exhaustive, and it says so out loud. Each reader stops at the most
    recent hundred sessions — a developer's profile holds hundreds, and the machine
    this was validated on held 842 — and when the cap takes anything, the line under
    the title names both numbers: a capped list presented as the whole history is the
    one thing a cap must not do.

    And one thing it is. It opens on the live sessions — Running or Stalled — because
    "what is going on right now" is the question somebody opens this for. What that
    rests on differs per agent: Claude writes a file per running session, Copilot's
    state is a timeout over a folder with no liveness marker, and the detail panel
    says so on every Copilot row.

    The filter bar holds every control that removes a row — Show, With delivery runs,
    Machine — so a reader who wonders why a session is missing finds every reason in
    one place, and Group by beside them moves rows and removes none, which is why the
    count badge does not move when the grouping does. Every filter comes back to its
    first option on every open: a filter that remembered itself would open the pane
    on a subset nobody asked for.

    The shell's repository scope reaches this list too, and it is the one filter this
    pane does not own a control for, because the control is in the header. A session
    is in scope by the repository its agent recorded, by the one this product resolved
    from its working folder lying inside a registered clone, or by the repository a
    run of it named. Claude records none, so the subtitle says what the scope rests on
    rather than letting a reader conclude Claude ran nothing.

    Two subtractions, two lines. The subtitle says what the *reading* left out — the
    cap, in the catalog's own numbers. The badge says what the *filters* are hiding,
    and names both numbers whenever they hide any.

    The rows are SessionRows, not sessions: a run file and a session record describe
    the same piece of work from two sides, either can be the one this PC still holds,
    and SessionRows.Of makes them one list. A run no listed session drove is a row of
    its own that says so.

    The ✕ only reports that it was pressed; what that closes is the shell's business.
*@

<section @key=@("sessions-pane") class="sessions-panel" id="sessions-pane" aria-labelledby="sessions-title" data-testid="sessions-panel">
    @* The library's section header wearing this pane's own class names, subtitle
       test id included — the capped-list wording is asserted through it. *@
    <SectionHeader BaseClass="sessions-panel__header"
                   TextCssClass=""
                   EyebrowCssClass="sessions-panel__eyebrow"
                   TitleCssClass="sessions-panel__title"
                   DescriptionCssClass="sessions-panel__subtitle"
                   DescriptionTestId="sessions-subtitle"
                   ActionsCssClass="sessions-panel__header-actions"
                   Eyebrow="Sessions"
                   TitleId="sessions-title"
                   Title="@Heading"
                   Description="@Subtitle">
        <Actions>
            @* It answers to the filters and not to the grouping: it stays put while
               Group by moves the same rows around, and it names both numbers the
               moment a filter leaves some of them out. *@
            <Badge BaseClass="sessions-panel__count" Kind="" TestId="sessions-count">@CountLabel</Badge>
            <IconButton AriaLabel="Close sessions pane" CssClass="btn--ghost" OnClick="() => OnClose.InvokeAsync()">✕</IconButton>
        </Actions>
    </SectionHeader>

    <div class="sessions-panel__filters" data-testid="sessions-filters">
        @* The filters first, because they decide which rows exist before Group by
           decides where they sit — left to right is the order the controls apply.

           Show is a one-of-many strip rather than a switch: a role="switch" states a
           boolean setting, and this resets to Live on every open; a strip that comes
           back to its first option reads as where you are looking. Live carries how
           many rows it would show under the other filters, so the press is never a
           guess. *@
        <div class="sessions-filter">
            <span class="sessions-filter__label">Show</span>
            <ButtonGroup AriaLabel="Which sessions to show" TestId="sessions-view-filter">
                @foreach (var view in Views)
                {
                    <ToggleButton Pressed="_view == view"
                                  PressedChanged="_ => ChooseView(view)"
                                  TestId="@($"sessions-view-{Slug(view)}")">
                        @AgentSessionViews.Label(view)
                        @if (view is AgentSessionView.Live)
                        {
                            <span class="sessions-filter__tally" data-testid="sessions-live-tally">@LiveTally</span>
                        }
                    </ToggleButton>
                }
            </ButtonGroup>
        </div>

        @* One toggle: only the rows with a delivery run on them, or every row. A
           filter like Show, so the badge moves when it is pressed. *@
        <ButtonGroup AriaLabel="Whether to show only rows with a delivery run" TestId="sessions-runs-filter">
            <ToggleButton Pressed="_withRuns"
                          PressedChanged="value => _withRuns = value"
                          TestId="sessions-runs-only">
                With delivery runs
            </ToggleButton>
        </ButtonGroup>

        @* "Machine", the dashboard's word for this same control, and a select for the
           reason the dashboard's is one: the options are however many machines have
           reported, which is not a list this pane can promise stays short. Read off
           the whole catalog, so an option is offered exactly when there are rows
           behind it, and named the way Group by machine names its sections. *@
        <div class="sessions-filter">
            <span class="sessions-filter__label">Machine</span>
            <SelectField CurrentValue="@_environmentId"
                         Options="@EnvironmentOptions"
                         Label="Machine to focus on"
                         IncludeEmptyOption="true"
                         EmptyLabel="All machines"
                         CssClass="badge badge--area"
                         TestId="sessions-machine-filter"
                         OnChanged="ChooseEnvironment" />
        </div>

        @* A select over a closed set of three, as the agreed canvas draws it. When
           first: it is the shape that puts the live rows on top and the rest under
           the day they were last active. *@
        <div class="sessions-filter">
            <span class="sessions-filter__label">Group by</span>
            <SelectField CurrentValue="@Slug(_grouping)"
                         Options="@GroupingOptions"
                         Label="How to group the sessions"
                         CssClass="badge badge--area"
                         TestId="sessions-grouping-filter"
                         OnChanged="ChooseGrouping" />
        </div>

        <div class="sessions-filter sessions-filter--end">
            @if (_keeper is not null)
            {
                @* Amends every one of this machine's session records from what its
                   agents' files still hold, and asks sync to send them all again when
                   sync is on. Beside Refresh because it is the heavier version of the
                   same question. *@
                <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Secondary"
                           Disabled="@(_loading || _updating)"
                           TestId="sessions-update-records"
                           Title="Re-read every record from the agents' files and send them to sync again"
                           OnClick="UpdateRecordsAsync">
                    @(_updating ? "Updating records..." : "Update records")
                </AppButton>
            }
            <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Secondary"
                       Disabled="@_loading"
                       TestId="sessions-refresh"
                       OnClick="RefreshAsync">
                @(_loading ? "Reading..." : "Refresh")
            </AppButton>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sessions-panel__content" id="sessions-content" aria-busy="@(_loading ? "true" : null)">
        @if (_recordsMessage is not null)
        {
            <Alert Message="@_recordsMessage" BaseClass="sessions-panel__notice" Role="status" TestId="sessions-records-updated" />
        }
        @if (FocusMessage is { } focusMessage)
        {
            <Alert Message="@focusMessage" BaseClass="sessions-panel__notice" Role="status" TestId="sessions-focus-missing" />
        }
        @if (Unreadable.Count > 0)
        {
            @* Named, not swallowed: one agent's folder being unreadable leaves the
               other's rows perfectly good, and a reader has to tell "no Copilot
               sessions" from "Copilot could not be read". The one notice here that is
               a failure, so it carries the read again as its Retry. *@
            <Alert Message="@UnreadableMessage"
                   BaseClass="sessions-panel__notice"
                   Role="alert"
                   ActionLabel="Retry"
                   OnAction="RefreshAsync"
                   ActionTestId="sessions-unreadable-retry"
                   TestId="sessions-unreadable" />
        }

        @* Total, not Shown: a refresh of a fully-filtered list is not a first read,
           and this placeholder would flash on every one of them. Placeholder rows
           rather than a sentence, because a list on its way is drawn in the shape of
           one. *@
        @if (_loading && Total == 0)
        {
            <div class="sessions-panel__loading" data-testid="sessions-loading" aria-hidden="true">
                @foreach (var width in SkeletonWidths)
                {
                    <Skeleton Shape="SkeletonShape.Block" Width="@width" />
                }
            </div>
        }
        else if (Shown == 0)
        {
            @* Nothing on this machine, or nothing these filters admit — two different
               facts, and the sentence under the title names the way back out. *@
            <EmptyState Title="@EmptyMessage" Description="@EmptyDescription" TestId="sessions-empty" />
        }
        else
        {
            // The sections and the row in the panel, worked out once per render: the
            // grouping sorts every row, and asking for it per row would sort the list
            // once for each of them.
            var sections = Sections;
            var selected = SelectedOf(sections);
            _shownKey = selected?.Key;

            <div class="sessions-layout">
                <section class="sessions-list" aria-label="Claude and Copilot sessions this PC has a record of" data-testid="sessions-list">
                    @foreach (var section in sections)
                    {
                        <div class="sessions-group" @key="@(section.Key ?? section.Name ?? "all")" data-testid="sessions-group">
                            @if (section.Name is not null)
                            {
                                <h3 class="sessions-group__heading">
                                    <span class="sessions-group__name" data-testid="sessions-group-name">@SectionName(section)</span>
                                    <span class="sessions-group__size" title="@SessionCount(section.Rows.Count)" data-testid="sessions-group-size">@section.Rows.Count</span>
                                </h3>
                            }
                            <ul class="sessions-group__rows">
                                @foreach (var row in section.Rows)
                                {
                                    <li @key="row.Key">
                                        @RowButton(row)
                                    </li>
                                }
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    }
                </section>

                @if (selected is not null)
                {
                    @Detail(selected)
                }
            </div>
        }
    </div>
</section>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// One row of the list, as a pressable button: pressing it shows the row in the
    /// detail panel. Three lines — who and how it stands, where and on what, and how
    /// far its run got — each of which a reader scanning the list is looking for,
    /// and nothing that is a way into something else: the pull requests and the task
    /// are in the panel, because a link inside a button is markup no browser agrees
    /// on.
    /// </summary>
    private RenderFragment RowButton(SessionRow row) => __builder =>
    {
        <ToggleButton BaseClass="sessions-row"
                      PressedCssClass="sessions-row--selected"
                      CssClass="@(IsFocused(row) ? "sessions-row--focused" : null)"
                      Pressed="@IsSelected(row)"
                      PressedChanged="_ => Select(row)"
                      TestId="sessions-row"
                      data-row-key="@row.Key"
                      @attributes="@FocusAttributes(row)">
            <span class="sessions-row__line">
                @* The mark alone on screen; the word for a screen reader and in the
                   title, so the mark is never the only carrier. *@
                <span class="sessions-row__kind" title="@AgentSessionGroups.Label(row.Kind)">
                    <ProviderMark Provider="@Provider(row.Kind)" Size="20" CssClass="sessions-row__mark" />
                    <span class="sr-only">@AgentSessionGroups.Label(row.Kind)</span>
                </span>
                <span class="@TitleClass(row)" title="@row.Title">@row.Title</span>
                <IntegrationStateChip Session="@State(row.State)" />
            </span>
            <span class="sessions-row__line sessions-row__facts">
                @* The repository wears its identity edge here, on the one fact that
                   names it — a rule down the whole row would read as if the session
                   belonged to that project. The em dash for a row that names none. *@
                <span class="@RepositoryClass(row)" title="@RepositoryTitle(row)" data-testid="sessions-repository">@Or(RepositoryLabel(row.Repository))</span>
                <span data-testid="sessions-machine">@row.Environment</span>
                <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                <span title="@Moment(row.LastActivityAt)" data-testid="sessions-last-activity">@Ago(row.LastActivityAt)</span>
                @if (DurationLabel(row.Duration) is { } duration)
                {
                    <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                    <span title="From its start to its last activity" data-testid="sessions-duration">@duration</span>
                }
                <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                <span class="sessions-row__model" data-testid="sessions-model">
                    @ModelLabel(row.Model)
                    <EffortChip Effort="@row.Effort" TestId="sessions-effort" />
                </span>
                <span class="sessions-row__spacer" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="sessions-row__tokens" title="@TokensTitle(row.Session?.ModelUsage)" data-testid="sessions-tokens">@OutputLabel(row.OutputTokens)</span>
            </span>
            @if (row.Runs.Count > 0)
            {
                @* The run the row last drove: one mark per stage and where it stands,
                   so how far it got is read without opening anything. A row of a
                   schedule's runs shows the latest of them. *@
                <span class="sessions-row__line">
                    <StageStrip Steps="@DeliveryRunProgress.Steps(row.Runs[0])"
                                Summary="@RunSummary(row)"
                                TestId="sessions-stage-strip" />
                </span>
            }
        </ToggleButton>
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// The detail panel of one row: its facts, the notes on where the record came
    /// from, the delivery run it drove, and the pull requests and task its work led
    /// to — in that order, which is the order a reader asks about a session in.
    /// </summary>
    private RenderFragment Detail(SessionRow row) => __builder =>
    {
        <aside class="sessions-detail" aria-label="Selected session" data-testid="sessions-detail" data-row-key="@row.Key">
            <div class="sessions-detail__head">
                <ProviderMark Provider="@Provider(row.Kind)" Size="28" CssClass="sessions-detail__mark" />
                <span class="sessions-detail__provider">
                    @AgentSessionGroups.Label(row.Kind)
                    @if (EntrypointLabel(row.Session?.Entrypoint) is { } entrypoint)
                    {
                        <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                        <Badge Kind="kind"
                               CssClass="sessions-detail__entrypoint"
                               Title="@($"Run from {row.Session!.Entrypoint}")"
                               TestId="sessions-entrypoint">@entrypoint</Badge>
                    }
                </span>
                <IntegrationStateChip Session="@State(row.State)" />
                <span class="sessions-detail__when" title="@Moment(row.LastActivityAt)">@Ago(row.LastActivityAt)</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="@($"sessions-detail__title {(IsIdentifierTitle(row) ? "data-table__mono" : string.Empty)}".Trim())" data-testid="sessions-detail-title">@row.Title</h3>

            @* Where the record came from, in the quiet register: nothing is wrong
               with any of these rows, and each sentence says what the row rests on
               and why something a local row has is not here. *@
            @if (row.RunOnly)
            {
                <p class="sessions-detail__note" data-testid="sessions-run-only">@RunOnlyLine(row)</p>
            }
            else if (row.Session!.Origin is AgentSessionOrigin.Replicated)
            {
                @* The machine's name and not its id, so the row survives greyscale and
                   reads out loud; a raw path from another disk stays behind by ADR
                   0005, and this sentence is why there is no folder below. *@
                <p class="sessions-detail__note" data-testid="sessions-origin">@OriginLine(row.Session)</p>
            }
            @if (row.Origin is AgentSessionOrigin.Recorded)
            {
                <p class="sessions-detail__note" data-testid="sessions-recorded">@RecordedLine</p>
            }
            @if (row.Kind is AgentSessionKind.Copilot)
            {
                <p class="sessions-detail__note" data-testid="sessions-copilot-liveness">@CopilotLivenessLine</p>
            }

            <dl class="sessions-detail__facts" data-testid="sessions-facts">
                <div class="sessions-fact">
                    <dt>Repository</dt>
                    <dd><span class="@RepositoryClass(row)" title="@RepositoryTitle(row)">@Or(RepositoryLabel(row.Repository))</span></dd>
                </div>
                <div class="sessions-fact">
                    <dt>Machine</dt>
                    <dd>@row.Environment</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="sessions-fact">
                    <dt>Model</dt>
                    <dd data-testid="sessions-fact-model" title="@row.Model">@ModelLabel(row.Model)</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="sessions-fact">
                    <dt>Effort</dt>
                    <dd data-testid="sessions-fact-effort">
                        @if (row.Effort is { } effort)
                        {
                            <EffortChip Effort="@effort" TestId="sessions-fact-effort-chip" />
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            @NotRecorded
                        }
                    </dd>
                </div>
                <div class="sessions-fact">
                    <dt>Started</dt>
                    <dd data-testid="sessions-started">@Moment(row.StartedAt)</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="sessions-fact">
                    <dt>Duration</dt>
                    <dd data-testid="sessions-fact-duration">@Or(DurationLabel(row.Duration))</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="sessions-fact">
                    <dt>Output</dt>
                    <dd data-testid="sessions-fact-output" title="@TokensTitle(row.Session?.ModelUsage)">@TokensCell(row.Session?.ModelUsage, row.OutputTokens)</dd>
                </div>
                @* What the session cost: Claude Code's reported figure, or estimated
                   from its runs' tokens at the Settings prices and marked so. With
                   neither there is no fact at all — a zero nobody measured would
                   read as free. *@
                @if (CostsOf(row)?.Session is { } cost)
                {
                    <div class="sessions-fact">
                        <dt>Cost</dt>
                        <dd data-testid="sessions-fact-cost" data-source="@(cost.Estimated ? "estimated" : "reported")" title="@DeliveryRunStages.CostTitle(cost)">
                            @cost.Label
                            @if (cost.Estimated)
                            {
                                <span class="sessions-fact__note">@CostFigure.EstimatedNote</span>
                            }
                        </dd>
                    </div>
                }
                @* The session's part of the week's telemetry cost, and once a weekly
                   refusal has sized the limit, an estimate of its part of that. *@
                @if (SharesOf(row) is { Session: { } share } shares)
                {
                    <div class="sessions-fact">
                        <dt>Share of week</dt>
                        <dd data-testid="sessions-fact-share">
                            <UsageShareFact Share="share" Usage="shares.Usage" TestId="sessions-share" />
                        </dd>
                    </div>
                }
                <div class="sessions-fact">
                    <dt>Branch</dt>
                    <dd class="data-table__mono" data-testid="sessions-branch">@Or(row.Branch)</dd>
                </div>
                @if (!row.RunOnly && row.Session!.Origin is not AgentSessionOrigin.Replicated && !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(row.WorkingFolder))
                {
                    <div class="sessions-fact sessions-fact--wide">
                        <dt>Working folder</dt>
                        <dd class="data-table__mono" data-testid="sessions-folder">@row.WorkingFolder</dd>
                    </div>
                }
            </dl>

            @if (row.Runs.Count > 0)
            {
                @* The run card: every run the row holds, latest first, each the line
                   that has always drawn a run — its references, its outcome, and the
                   fold with its stages and figures. *@
                <section class="sessions-detail__card" aria-label="Delivery runs" data-testid="sessions-run-card">
                    <h4 class="sessions-detail__card-title">@(row.Runs.Count == 1 ? "Delivery run" : $"Delivery runs · {row.Runs.Count}")</h4>
                    <div class="sessions-runs" data-testid="sessions-runs">
                        @foreach (var run in row.Runs)
                        {
                            <DeliveryRunLine @key="@($"{run.Dashboard}/{run.Worktree}/{run.Id}")" Run="run" References="@ReferencesOf(row, run)" Costs="@CostsOf(row)?.StagesOf(run)" Comparison="@CostsOf(row)?.ComparisonOf(run)" OnOpenTask="OnOpenTask">
                                <Usage>
                                    <UsageShareFact Share="@SharesOf(row)?.Of(run)" Usage="@SharesOf(row)?.Usage" Run="true" TestId="sessions-run-share" />
                                </Usage>
                            </DeliveryRunLine>
                        }
                    </div>
                </section>
            }
            else
            {
                <p class="sessions-detail__card sessions-detail__note" data-testid="sessions-no-run">@NoRunLine</p>
            }

            <section class="sessions-detail__produced" aria-label="What it produced">
                <h4 class="sessions-detail__section-title">What it produced</h4>
                <div class="sessions-detail__cards">
                    <div class="sessions-detail__card" data-testid="sessions-pull-request-card">
                        <span class="sessions-detail__card-label">Pull request</span>
                        @if (PullRequestsOf(row) is { Count: > 0 } pulls)
                        {
                            @foreach (var pull in pulls)
                            {
                                <div class="sessions-detail__work" data-testid="sessions-pull-requests">
                                    <IntegrationLink Link="@DeliveryRunLine.Link(pull)"
                                                     ShowTitle="false"
                                                     CssClass="sessions-detail__link"
                                                     TestId="sessions-pull-request" />
                                    @if (PullTitle(pull) is { } title)
                                    {
                                        <span class="sessions-detail__work-title" title="@title">@title</span>
                                    }
                                    @if (StatusOf(pull) is { } status)
                                    {
                                        <Badge Kind="tone"
                                               Slug="@ToneSlug(status.Tone)"
                                               Title="@status.Reason"
                                               CssClass="sessions-detail__verdict"
                                               TestId="sessions-pull-request-verdict">@status.Label</Badge>
                                    }
                                </div>
                            }
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <span class="sessions-detail__none">No pull request yet.</span>
                        }
                    </div>
                    <div class="sessions-detail__card" data-testid="sessions-task-card">
                        <span class="sessions-detail__card-label">Task</span>
                        @if (TaskOf(row) is { } task)
                        {
                            <div class="sessions-detail__work">
                                <IntegrationLink Link="@TaskLink(task)"
                                                 ShowTitle="false"
                                                 OnOpen="@TaskOpener(task)"
                                                 TestId="sessions-task" />
                                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(task.Title))
                                {
                                    <span class="sessions-detail__work-title" title="@task.Title">@task.Title</span>
                                }
                            </div>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <span class="sessions-detail__none">No task names this session.</span>
                        }
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>
        </aside>
    };

    /// <summary>The views on offer, Live first because it is the one the pane opens in.</summary>
    private static readonly AgentSessionView[] Views =
    [
        AgentSessionView.Live,
        AgentSessionView.All
    ];

    /// <summary>The groupings on offer, in the order the select lists them. When
    /// first, because it is the shape the list has when the pane opens.</summary>
    private static readonly AgentSessionGrouping[] Groupings =
    [
        AgentSessionGrouping.When,
        AgentSessionGrouping.Repository,
        AgentSessionGrouping.Environment
    ];

    private static readonly IReadOnlyList<SelectorOption> GroupingOptions =
        [.. Groupings.Select(grouping => new SelectorOption(Slug(grouping), GroupingLabel(grouping)))];

    /// <summary>An em dash: the agent did not record this.</summary>
    private const string Missing = "—";

    /// <summary>What a fact nobody recorded reads, where an em dash would be too
    /// quiet to tell from a value: the model and the effort, the two facts a reader
    /// compares sessions on.</summary>
    private const string NotRecorded = "not recorded";

    private AgentSessionCatalog _catalog = AgentSessionCatalog.Empty;

    /// <summary>The runs, and the one list the two readings make together — built
    /// once per read, because it hashes every session's folder against every
    /// worktree a run was filed under, and a render happens on every press.</summary>
    private DeliveryRunCatalog _runs = DeliveryRunCatalog.Empty;
    private IReadOnlyList<SessionRow> _rows = [];
    private AgentSessionView _view = AgentSessionView.Live;

    /// <summary>Whether only the rows with a delivery run on them are shown. Off on
    /// every open, like the view.</summary>
    private bool _withRuns;

    private AgentSessionGrouping _grouping = AgentSessionGrouping.When;

    /// <summary>The environment the list is narrowed to, by id, or null for all of
    /// them. Back to all on every open.</summary>
    private string? _environmentId;

    /// <summary>The row the reader picked, by key, or null for none picked yet —
